# Line-ending and binary rules.
#
# This file exists mainly for the committed Android project. Without it, the
# stored line endings of the Gradle wrapper depend on each contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf`, and a `gradlew` committed with CRLF makes Linux CI fail with
# `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` before Gradle ever starts -- a confusing failure
# that looks nothing like its cause.

# The wrapper is a POSIX shell script on Linux and macOS runners.
webapp/android/gradlew text eol=lf
# Its Windows counterpart is a batch file and needs CRLF.
webapp/android/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Gradle and Android build inputs are text and should normalise to LF.
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.pro text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. Git usually infers this,
# but signing material and archives are too costly to get wrong silently.
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary
*.pdf binary
